==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*erlaz}}, further origin unknown. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term/t|osx|erl}}, Old High German {{term/t|goh|erl}}, Old Norse {{term/t|non|jarl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/eorl/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# Anglo-Saxon of noble rank; a nobleman ranking above a [[thane]]; [[alderman]]
# [[warrior]], brave man
# Danish under-king, [[jarl]]

